    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 22-layer planar multilayer filter on CaF2 substrate with Air incidence. Stack sequence: Air | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | ZnS | MgF2 | CaF2. All 22 layer thicknesses are optimization variables. Apply physics-constrained initialization: clamp all cavity and spacer layer thicknesses to [50, 150] nm range before gradient optimization begins. Use gradient_thickness optimizer with uniform physical bounds. Score candidates on transmittance: high in 3250-3350 nm and 4200-4300 nm bands, low in 2500-3100 nm and 4450-5000 nm bands. Normal incidence, unpolarized illumination. No metal layers permitted. Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 2500-3100 nm, 3250-3350 nm, 4200-4300 nm, 4450-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 3.25-3.35 um and 4.20-4.30 um bands; Low transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 2.50-3.10 um and 4.45-5.00 um bands. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count <= 24; No metal layers; Conventional depositable infrared inorganic dielectric materials only.",
